NNAAMMEE
     ddeevv__mmkkddbb — create /dev database

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddeevv__mmkkddbb

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevv__mmkkddbb command creates a hash(3) access method Berkeley database in
     “_/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_d_e_v_._d_b” which contains the names of all of the character and
     block special files in the “_/_d_e_v” directory, using the file type and the
     _s_t___r_d_e_v field as the key.

     Keys are a structure containing a _m_o_d_e___t followed by a _d_e_v___t, with any
     padding zeroed out.  The former is the type of the file (_s_t___m_o_d_e &
     S_IFMT), the latter is the _s_t___r_d_e_v field.

FFIILLEESS
     /dev             device directory
     /var/run/dev.db  database file

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ps(1), stat(2), dbopen(3), devname(3), kvm_nlist(3), ttyname(3),
     kvm_mkdb(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ddeevv__mmkkddbb command appeared in 4.3BSD Net/2.

